# 🤖 Automated Daily LinkedIn Posts via Notion – Complete Workflow Guide

This workflow automates your daily LinkedIn posting process using Notion as the content source. It fetches the day's post, formats the content (including images), publishes it to LinkedIn, and updates the post status in Notion.

---

## ✅ Prerequisites

- **Notion Integration**: Create an integration in [Notion](https://www.notion.so/my-integrations) and add it to your workspace.
- **LinkedIn Page Access**: Ensure you have admin access to the LinkedIn Company Page.
- **Automation Platform**: Use [n8n](https://n8n.io/) or [Make](https://www.make.com/).
- **Image Hosting**: Use a service like Imgur, AWS S3, or similar for image uploads.

---

## 🧱 Workflow Overview

1. **Trigger**: Daily at scheduled time (e.g., 9 AM)
2. **Fetch Post**: Retrieve today's post from Notion
3. **Process Content**: Format text and upload images
4. **Publish to LinkedIn**
5. **Update Notion Status**

---

## 🔧 Step-by-Step Setup

### 1. Notion Database Setup

Create a Notion database with the following fields:

| Field Name     | Type         | Description                        |
|----------------|--------------|------------------------------------|
| Title          | Title        | Post headline                      |
| Content        | Text         | Main body of the post              |
| Image URL      | URL          | Link to image (optional)           |
| Date           | Date         | Scheduled publish date             |
| Status         | Select       | Options: Draft, Published, Failed  |
| LinkedIn ID    | Text         | Auto-filled after publishing       |

---

### 2. Automation Platform Setup (n8n Example)

#### Node 1: Schedule Trigger
- Set to run daily at desired time (e.g., 09:00 AM)

#### Node 2: Notion – Get Today's Post
```javascript
const today = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
const response = await $http.request('GET', 
  `https://api.notion.com/v1/databases/YOUR_DATABASE_ID/query`, {
  headers: {
    'Authorization': `Bearer YOUR_NOTION_TOKEN`,
    'Notion-Version': '2022-06-28'
  },
  query: {
    filter: {
      property: 'Date',
      date: { equals: today }
    },
    status: { select: { equals: 'Draft' } }
  }
});
return response.data.results[0];
```

#### Node 3: Process Content & Upload Image
```javascript
const post = $input.item.json;
let imageUrl = null;

if (post.properties['Image URL'].url) {
  const imageResponse = await $http.request('POST', 'https://api.imgur.com/3/image', {
    headers: { Authorization: 'Client-ID YOUR_IMGUR_CLIENT_ID' },
    formData: { image: post.properties['Image URL'].url }
  });
  imageUrl = imageResponse.data.link;
}

const content = post.properties.Content.rich_text.map(t => t.plain_text).join('\n');
return { title: post.properties.Title.title[0].plain_text, content, imageUrl };
```

#### Node 4: Publish to LinkedIn
```javascript
const post = $input.item.json;
const response = await $http.request('POST', 
  'https://api.linkedin.com/v2/ugcPosts', {
  headers: {
    'Authorization': `Bearer YOUR_LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN`,
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'X-Restli-Protocol-Version': '2.0.0'
  },
  json: {
    author: 'urn:li:organization:YOUR_COMPANY_PAGE_ID',
    commentary: `${post.content}`,
    visibility: 'ANYONE',
    distribution: { feedDistribution: 'MAIN_FEED' }
  }
});
return response.data;
```

#### Node 5: Update Notion Status
```javascript
const post = $('Get Post').item.json;
const linkedinId = $input.item.json.id;

await $http.request('PATCH', 
  `https://api.notion.com/v1/pages/${post.id}`, {
  headers: {
    'Authorization': `Bearer YOUR_NOTION_TOKEN`,
    'Notion-Version': '2022-06-28'
  },
  json: {
    properties: {
      Status: { select: { name: 'Published' } },
      'LinkedIn ID': { rich_text: [{ text: { content: linkedinId } }] }
    }
  }
});
return { success: true, pageId: post.id };
```

